        <dictScrap type="liebermann"><hi rend="bold">folcland</hi> <hi rend="italic">volksrechtliches Grundeigen, gemeines, landrechtl., nicht eximirtes, im <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Gegensatz"><abbr>Ggs.</abbr></ref> zum Besitzrecht des</hi> bocland, <hi rend="italic">des vom König privilegirten Grundeigens</hi> [<hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:vergleiche"><abbr>vgl</abbr></ref>. die Bedeutung von</hi> folc <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Nummer"><abbr>n.</abbr></ref></hi> 2, <hi rend="italic">in</hi> folcgerihtu, folcriht <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Nummer"><abbr>n.</abbr></ref></hi> 1b <hi rend="italic">und in</hi> Old <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:english"><abbr>Engl.</abbr></ref> Bede <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:editio"><abbr>ed.</abbr></ref> </hi><ref type="bibl" target="bib:CitMillerBede"><hi rend="italic">Miller</hi> I 326</ref>: ondred ondettan, þæt he cyninges þegn wære; <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:accusativus"><abbr>ac</abbr></ref> sæde, þæt he folclic mon wære <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:fur"><abbr>für</abbr></ref></hi> Bæda IV 22: timuit se militem fuisse confiteri; rusticum se fuisse respondit]; <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Dativ"><abbr>dt</abbr></ref>:</hi> ~de <ref type="lawCode" target="law:IEw">I Ew</ref> 2. 2,1; <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:unubersetzt"><abbr>unübs</abbr></ref></hi> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Quadr">Q</ref>, <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:auch"><abbr>auch</abbr></ref></hi> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Rb">Rb</ref> <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Seite"><abbr>S.</abbr></ref></hi> 139*</dictScrap>
